    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d253">

                <pb facs="0269" n="195" xml:id="pg195"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/824</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Langhorne</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-09-07T17:00:00+01:19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 7, 1917, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 9.40 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1319. Legation informed that it is the opinion in German circles in Holland that
                    general effect of President’s reply to Pope’s message will be to temporarily
                    retard democratic reform in Germany and that the note has furnished new fighting
                    material to the Conservatives and the military party.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Langhorne</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
